\\ A peer program that does NOT include examples/remote/ledger.decl.fen: it
\\ declares Ledger itself, with one operation more than the shared file has.
\\ It serves everything the ledger caller performs, in the right modes, so the
\\ only thing wrong with a system of that caller and this peer is that the two
\\ were built from different declarations of Ledger. Their signature digests
\\ differ, and the supervisor refuses to assemble the system (EFFECTS.md §12.6;
\\ owner ruling of 16 November 2026 on §12.10 question 15). The build makes an
\\ image of this program beside the real peer so that the refusal can be shown.

(remote-effect Ledger
  (add I64 --> (Tuple I64 I64))
  (read-only total Unit --> I64)
  (read-only entries Unit --> I64))

(serve Ledger
  ((add key amount) -> (do (perform StoreWrite put 0 (+ (perform StoreRead get 0) amount))
                           (perform StoreWrite put 1 (+ (perform StoreRead get 1) 1))
                           (tuple 0 (perform StoreRead get 0))))
  ((total u) -> (perform StoreRead get 0))
  ((entries u) -> (perform StoreRead get 1)))
